Open Router3 → **CLI** tab, press Enter, then paste this:

```
enable
configure terminal
interface g0/0
 ip address 10.0.3.2 255.255.255.252
 no shutdown
interface g0/1
 ip address 10.0.4.1 255.255.255.252
 no shutdown
exit
router ospf 1
 network 10.0.3.0 0.0.0.3 area 0
 network 10.0.4.0 0.0.0.3 area 0
end
write memory
```

Check with `show ip interface brief`. The R0–R3 link should turn up/up now. The R3–R2 link stays down until Router2 is configured, which is the last one.
